<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">{{ site.researchByUrl[page.url].kicker }}</p>
  <h1>Entropy and the Phases of Integration</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">Entropy is a family of precise quantities. &ldquo;Integration&rdquo; is TTI&rsquo;s proposed
    metaphysical reading of how settled structure gathers. They may be compared; they must not be equated.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--first illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">The governing distinction</p>
    <h2 id="t-two-ledgers">One Word from Physics, One Proposal from TTI</h2>
    <p><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> In equilibrium statistical mechanics, entropy counts accessible
      microstates relative to a stated macro-description. In thermodynamics it is a state function whose
      changes constrain possible processes. In information theory it measures uncertainty in a distribution.
      Those definitions are related, but not interchangeable without assumptions.</p>
    <p><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> TTI uses <em>integration</em> for a different idea: degrees of freedom
      becoming able to act as a coherent whole. That can be a useful organising image. No established law says
      that a higher TTI integration phase has lower entropy, more consciousness, more mass or a particular
      cosmological abundance.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap reveal">
  <div class="grid two">
    <article class="frame card">
      <p class="kicker">Established &middot; statistical</p>
      <h2 id="t-boltzmann">Boltzmann&rsquo;s Count</h2>
      <p class="formula">\[S=k_{\mathrm B}\ln\Omega\]</p>
      <p>Here \(\Omega\) is the number of microstates compatible with a specified macrostate. The formula
        does not say that disorder is a substance. It says that a coarse description can be realised in many
        microscopic ways. Change the constraints or the coarse-graining and the count can change.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card">
      <p class="kicker">Established &middot; thermodynamic</p>
      <h2 id="t-second-law">The Second Law</h2>
      <p class="formula">\[\Delta S_{\mathrm{isolated}}\geq 0\]</p>
      <p>For an isolated macroscopic system, entropy does not spontaneously decrease. Local order may grow
        while the surroundings gain still more entropy. Life, crystals and galaxies therefore do not refute
        the law: none is an isolated box, and gravitational systems require particular care.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card">
      <p class="kicker">Established &middot; quantum</p>
      <h2 id="t-von-neumann">A Density Matrix Has Entropy</h2>
      <p class="formula">\[S(\rho)=-k_{\mathrm B}\,\mathrm{Tr}(\rho\ln\rho)\]</p>
      <p>A closed quantum state can evolve unitarily while subsystem entropy rises through entanglement.
        Decoherence can make interference inaccessible in practice without adding a literal collapse to the
        unitary equation. This is not, by itself, TTI integration or conscious gathering.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card">
      <p class="kicker">Established &middot; informational</p>
      <h2 id="t-shannon">Uncertainty Is Not Heat</h2>
      <p class="formula">\[H(X)=-\sum_i p_i\log p_i\]</p>
      <p>Shannon entropy quantifies expected surprise. Converting it into a thermodynamic cost requires a
        physical implementation and a protocol, as in erasure. Similar formulae do not license the claim that
        meaning, spirit or awareness is simply thermodynamic entropy.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

